<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orihuela</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orihuela is a city in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alicante">Alicante</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the Segura river. It is the first of the seven towns named in the treaty of 713 between Theodemir and the Muslim conquerors, and it may have been his seat, giving the region of Tudmir its centre. It became part of the Crown of Aragon in the late 13th century, and an episcopal see was established there in 1564.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orihuela.jpg" alt="Orihuela" width="320" height="403" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Olecense · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Conjunto_hist%C3%B3rico_de_Orihuela.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
